{"name":"Prune Plum","hex":"#211640","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prune plum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of freestone plum suitable for making prunes (Prunus domestica subsp. domestica)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prune_plum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prune plum","blocks":[{"text":"The prune plum is a fruit-bearing tree, or its fruit. It is a subspecies of the plum Prunus domestica. The freestone fruit is especially popular in Central Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/20110718Prunus_domestica_subsp._domestica.jpg/330px-20110718Prunus_domestica_subsp._domestica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prune_plum"},{"title":"Prune","blocks":[{"text":"A prune is a dried plum, most commonly from the European plum tree. Not all plum species or varieties can be dried into prunes. Use of the term prune for fresh plums is obsolete except when applied to varieties of plum grown for drying. In this usage, a prune is the firm-fleshed plum fruit of P. domestica varieties that have a high soluble solids content and do not ferment during drying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Rosales_-_Dried_Prunus_domestica_d.jpg/330px-Rosales_-_Dried_Prunus_domestica_d.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prune"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum"},{"title":"Plum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum is a purple color with a brownish-gray tinge, like that shown on the right, or a reddish purple, which is a close representation of the average color of the plum fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Plum_on_tree02.jpg/330px-Plum_on_tree02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Cacaks_Beste.JPG/250px-Cacaks_Beste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Cacaks_Beste.JPG/500px-Cacaks_Beste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Cacaks_Beste.JPG/250px-Cacaks_Beste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACacaks_Beste.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Prunus_-_Elena.JPG/250px-Prunus_-_Elena.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Prunus_-_Elena.JPG/500px-Prunus_-_Elena.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Prunus_-_Elena.JPG/250px-Prunus_-_Elena.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrunus_-_Elena.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Prunus_-_Hauszwetschge.JPG/250px-Prunus_-_Hauszwetschge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Prunus_-_Hauszwetschge.JPG/500px-Prunus_-_Hauszwetschge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"